{"type":"message","id":"f79a5026","parentId":"2215cbc6","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:20:02.784Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sat 2026-03-28 12:20 GMT+8] RSS feed aggregator and reader\n\nBuild a web-based RSS feed aggregator that can add/remove feeds, fetch articles, mark as read, and display articles in a clean card layout. Use mock feed data.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n- Prefer these skill slugs for this task when relevant:\n  - find-skills\n- Before starting, search/install missing recommended skills in the current workspace when the runtime supports it.\n- Prefer exact ClawHub/OpenClaw skill slugs over vague descriptions whenever possible.\n\n## TeamClaw Git Collaboration\n- TeamClaw manages a git-backed project workspace for this task.\n- Sync mode: bundle.\n- Default branch: main.\n- Current HEAD: 65ed3f825fbf5085de23b7cd0c805089f718585b \"chore(teamclaw): checkpoint mn9sslzk-27bkgh (developer)\".\n- TeamClaw syncs the workspace checkout before task execution when needed.\n- Treat the current workspace as the canonical repo checkout; do not delete `.git` or replace the repo with ad-hoc archives.\n\n## Task Context\nReference: mn9ssm7o-v8ptxv\nAssigned Role: Developer\n\n## Execution Rules\n- Deliver exactly the artifact requested by this task.\n- Follow the task verb literally: if the task asks for a brief, plan, matrix, review, package, positioning, or design artifact, produce that artifact and stop there.\n- Do NOT scaffold code, project structure, configs, or files unless the task explicitly asks for implementation work.\n- Do NOT create additional tasks, task trees, or duplicate follow-up work.\n- Do NOT re-scope this into a multi-role coordination workflow.\n- Do NOT delegate the core work of this task away to another role.\n- If Task Context includes recent completed deliverables, treat them as upstream inputs and search the shared workspace for any referenced task IDs or filenames before requesting clarification.\n- Do NOT attempt to inspect or resolve another worker's OpenClaw session or session key; those sessions are isolated per worker.\n- If the task includes a Recommended Skills section, use those skills first and prefer the exact listed slugs when searching for additional help.\n- Do NOT mark the task completed or failed via progress tools. Return the final deliverable (or raise an error) and let TeamClaw close the task.\n- If critical information is missing and you cannot proceed safely, request clarification and wait instead of guessing.\n- If more work is needed, mention it briefly in your result or use a handoff/review tool on this same task.\n- Use structured fields on progress, review, handoff, and messaging tools whenever coordination is needed.\n- When naming a role, use exact TeamClaw role IDs: pm, architect, developer, qa, release-engineer, infra-engineer, devops, security-engineer, designer, marketing.\n- Do NOT use sessions_yield or end your turn while background work, coding agents, or process sessions are still running; if the task is not complete yet, reply with exactly TEAMCLAW_STILL_WAITING.\n- Never return 'running in background' as the final result for a TeamClaw task. If you spawn a helper session, keep monitoring it and only return after you have the actual deliverable.\n\n## Required: Submit a Result Contract\nYou MUST call teamclaw_submit_result_contract before finishing. This is how you report back to the team.\n- Provide a concise summary of what you built or found.\n- List each deliverable (file, directory, or artifact) with its path.\n- For web applications: set artifactType to \"web-app\", provide previewCommand (e.g. \"npx -y serve -l {PORT}\"), previewCwd (the project directory), and previewReadyPath (default \"/\").\n- For non-web deliverables (CLI tools, APIs, libraries, documents): omit artifactType — just list the files.\n- If blocked or blocked: list blockers. If follow-up is needed: list followUps with target roles."}],"timestamp":177467160278